The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
u8 __iomem ports[] = {
	idio16gpio->reg->out0_7, idio16gpio->reg->out8_15,
	idio16gpio->reg->in0_7, idio16gpio->reg->in8_15,
};
```
Reason:
The `ports` array was incorrectly defined as `u8 __iomem`, which does not correctly represent the memory addresses of the device I/O registers. This led to passing incorrect memory offsets to the `ioread8` function, causing improper access to the device I/O registers during the `get_multiple` callback.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
void __iomem *ports[] = {
	&idio16gpio->reg->out0_7, &idio16gpio->reg->out8_15,
	&idio16gpio->reg->in0_7, &idio16gpio->reg->in8_15,
};
```
Reason:
The `ports` array is now correctly defined as `void __iomem *`, which allows it to hold the proper memory addresses of the device I/O registers. This ensures that the correct memory offsets are passed to the `ioread8` function, allowing for proper access to the device I/O registers during the `get_multiple` callback.

